abstract: >-
  The RCM-CRM is an open-source Community Relationship
  Management (CRM) system for Research Community Managers,
  developed by RCM Cooperative. It supports transparent,
  privacy-conscious and UK GDPR-aware tracking of community
  engagement, and is designed to be cloned and adapted by
  any research community. The current build uses Baserow,
  with servers hosted in Germany, as a five-table relational
  database (People, Organisations, Communities,
  Interactions, Projects). A set of Claude Code skills
  ingests meeting notes, email contacts and Slack exports,
  and exports consent-filtered network visualisations to
  Kumu. Skills that process live CRM data use deterministic
  code rather than an LLM, and LLM use is limited to
  non-confidential source material. The repository also
  contains step-by-step training documentation, a data
  privacy impact assessment template, a platform needs
  assessment, and a consent model offering members five
  levels of data visibility. Documentation is released under
  CC-BY 4.0 and code under MIT.
